VERDICT: PASS
===========================================================================
  Two numbered hardware IP ACLs in the 3000 range, both bound to one port:
      access-list 3000 deny   ip 10.1.1.0 0.0.0.255 any   -> "deny ip 10.1.1.0/24 any"
      access-list 3001 permit ip any any
      interface port2.0.2 / access-group 3000 / access-group 3001

  "Traffic behaviour should be correct for each type of ACL"
      IPv4 source inside 10.1.1.0/24   base 10/10 -> 0/10   denied
      IPv4 source outside it           base 10/10 -> 10/10  permitted
      IPv6                             base 10/10 -> 10/10  unaffected by an IP ACL
      ARP (non-IP)                     base 10/10 -> 10/10  unaffected
      Counters confirm the permit rule taking hits, so both lists are live.

  Multiple access-groups coexist on one port and are evaluated together --
  the deny in 3000 wins over the permit-any in 3001 for matching traffic,
  which is the first-match behaviour across lists.

